{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"frouzy-downfallen-salamander","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`make lint` fails when a per-session scratch directory holds a virtualenv. `scripts/check_shellcheck.py::discover` walks `root.rglob(\"*.sh\")` and skips only the names in `EXCLUDED_DIRS` (`.venv`, `.git`, `.claude`, `.tickets-tracker`, `.tickets-hotpath-authoritative`, `node_modules`). Its comment says agent scratch is never linted, but `.rebar/scratch/` (the scratch path AGENTS.md prescribes) is not excluded, and a venv not literally named `.venv` is not either.\n\nObserved 2026-11-03 in worktree `fix-langur`: a non-editable reproduction venv at `.rebar/scratch/a85e3cd3-langur/nonedit-venv` made `make lint` exit 2 with SC2050 in `site-packages/virtualenv/activation/bash/activate.sh`. Removing the venv made `make lint` exit 0. The path is git-ignored (`.gitignore:23: .rebar/*`).\n\n## Approach\n\nExclude git-ignored paths from discovery, or at minimum add `.rebar` to `EXCLUDED_DIRS`, so the linter only judges shell the repository owns.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test places a `*.sh` file with a shellcheck warning under `.rebar/scratch/<x>/` in a temp root and asserts `discover` does not return it.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0 with a virtualenv present under `.rebar/scratch/`.\n\nFound while resolving `targeted-northbound-langur` (session a85e3cd3).","id":"d552-a55e-2877-47ef","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"check_shellcheck lints git-ignored .rebar/scratch, so a scratch venv fails make lint"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793719255701691001,"uuid":"be30d410-c446-4641-b35a-6f8cca3f76be"}